B.al9=new A.qJ("What stays on the device","Puzzle scores, lesson progress, visit-day count, audio and reminder settings, chosen home and study nationalities (country codes only), an optional Chinese given-name preference, and similar preferences are stored locally (SharedPreferences and app-private files). You can erase learning progress with Reset all progress in Settings. Nationality choices and a saved Chinese name stay on this device until you change them.",null)
B.ala=new A.qJ("Reminders","Grove recall reminders are off until you turn them on. If you enable them, the app asks for notification permission and schedules local notifications on this device. Scheduling uses your device time zone. Reminder settings are not uploaded.",null)
B.alb=new A.qJ("Network","Fonts, speech, and course data are bundled in the app. A release build uses the internet to upload the study log and, when you tap Send, a problem report. The study log goes out on the first open of a new day, or sooner if you tap Send study log now. Puzzle time in that log counts only while the puzzle is on screen and the app is open. The uploads are stored in Google Cloud Firestore for the developer of Hanzi Tree.",null)
B.alc=new A.mF("Language",u.ae,null)
B.ald=new A.qJ("Problem reports","On a release build, each puzzle has a Report a problem link. If you send one, the app includes the lesson, the puzzle line in that lesson's course file, the course file name, and the note you write (up to 300 characters). It uses the same anonymous id as the study log. Nothing is sent unless you tap Send. The developer is emailed a copy of each report you send.",null)
B.ale=new A.mF("One visit","Opening a lesson starts one visit. Class Tree, HSK, and Lin Mode all use the same visit.\n\nRegular round \u2014 you see every card in the set once. Each finished card adds a segment to the bar along the bottom of the screen. Teal means that card was right. Purple means it was missed.\n\nCatchup round \u2014 misses from the regular round come back once, and the screen flashes \u201cCatchup round!\u201d. A clean regular round ends the visit with no catchup. On the catchup pass the bar switches to a cooler teal when you get a card right, and burgundy when you miss it again.\n\nOn the lesson list, that same bar stays under the card: regular colors first, then the catchup colors, so the whole visit stays visible. Hover or press and hold the bar to see how many were right, such as 30/37.\n\nWhen the visit finishes, the lesson goes to sleep and its card dims. Stars under the title come from the regular round. More stars mean a longer rest: a few days at first, then about a week, two weeks, and a month. Five stars means the lesson is mastered and stays asleep. A weaker regular round keeps fewer stars, so it wakes sooner. You can still open a sleeping lesson, or hide sleeping lessons from the list.",null)
B.alf=new A.mF("Class Tree","The home screen lists classroom lessons. Tap a row to play. Switch between the list and a tree map with the Tree / List control.\n\nA dim card is resting. An item that looks locked is still ahead in the suggested order. You can open either one and drill anyway.\n\nOn the tree map, a ring fills teal as you finish visits, then a gold overlay tracks mastery stars.",null)
B.alg=new A.mF("Top bar","Tree \u2014 Class Tree, the home curriculum.\nHSK \u2014 HSK textbook lessons.\nLeaf \u2014 Learning Garden (what you have learned so far).\n\u6797 \u2014 Lin Mode textbook chapters.\nGrid \u2014 Character progress for the whole tree or the lesson you are in.\nGear \u2014 Settings, including the older Learning Tree and other test features.",null)
B.alh=new A.mF("Lin Mode","\u6797 opens textbook chapters beside Class Tree and HSK. Each card shows the chapter number, an icon, the English title, and the Chinese title under it, with a few sample words on the right. Visits, the color bar, and sleep work the same way as the other lesson lists.",null)
B.ali=new A.mF("During a round","Tap an answer. Correct slots light up; a wrong pick shows the right answer so you can compare. Fill every slot, or pick the matching choice, then tap Continue.\n\nIn a lesson, Help may open that lesson's intro first \u2014 use the link there for these general notes.",null)
B.alj=new A.mF("Character origins",u.dw,null)
B.alk=new A.mF("Lesson types","Foundations & Tutorial \u2014 tap IDS pieces to assemble the character.\nPictographs \u2014 pick the right hanzi for the clue (no assembly).\nRadicals \u2014 pick the matching component or glyph.\nOther nodes \u2014 compounds, opposites, numbers, colors, and themed word sets use the style shown when you open them.",null)
B.all=new A.qJ("What we do not collect","No account, email, or password. No contacts, camera, microphone, photos, or location GPS. An optional Chinese given name you choose stays on this device and is not an account or legal name. No advertising ID and no ads. No crash reporting. The study log does not include your name. A problem report is sent only when you tap Send.",null)
B.alm=new A.qJ("Study log","Each finished puzzle stores its result and the time it stayed on screen in the foreground. When you leave a lesson, that run is kept on this device. A release build sends the runs it has not sent yet on the first open of a new day, or when you tap Send study log now in Settings. A random id on this device groups those days together. The log has no name, and it is untraceable to you.",null)
